{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Pre-sweep against origin/main `d74d53a5ffd` — AC1 corrected before spending a gate slot.\n\n**AC1 could not pass on a correct implementation.** It required \"each of the six files\" to gain exactly one new `> **…**` blockquote. The Approach adds a blockquote to only five — 0010, 0013, 0029, 0057, 0092. **0083's change is a Status-line rewrite at `:5-6`, not a blockquote.** An implementer following the Approach exactly would have failed AC1 at close; one following AC1 would have added a blockquote to 0083 that the Approach never asked for. AC1 now names the five, states 0083's exemption explicitly, and points at AC3 as 0083's check.\n\nAC1 also said to verify with `sed -n '2,6p'`. For 0010 the new blockquote lands at `:5` (after the existing `> **Number note (story 0743):**` at `:3`, before `**Status:**`), which that range only just covers; widened to `sed -n '1,8p'` so the title and the Status line are both visible in the check.\n\n**Every other citation resolves.** Re-measured and recorded in the description's new section: 0010 title `:1` / number-note `:3` / Status `:5`; 0013, 0029, 0057, 0092 all carry `**Status:**` at `:3`; 0029's \"before the redesign\" is at `:5`; 0083's renumber blockquote is at `:3` with Status at `:5-6` and \"Phase 2 in progress under epic bbf1-82e1-cf9d-494a\" on `:5` (so AC3's grep finds it today); 0092's \"Keep explicit compatibility adapters\" paragraph is at `:24-27` and the file is exactly 56 lines, so the `## Amendment` section appends at the end as planned. `0021:3` and `0020:3` are the Status lines recording the amendments to 0010 and 0013.\n\nNo scope change; the six files and the Approach text are unchanged apart from AC1."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793473542125785001,"uuid":"ee1348c1-c6e0-4327-952f-a61af31a7fbb"}